Me:
what is pseudocode and why do we write it before coding

AI:
Pseudocode is a way of planning your code in plain English before you actually write it in Python. It shows the logic and structure without worrying about syntax.

Bad pseudocode — too vague:
  load the file
  clean it
  return data

Good pseudocode — right level of detail:
  FUNCTION load_and_clean(file):
    TRY to read file as CSV
    IF columns are missing: RAISE error
    REMOVE $ from Amount using regex
    CONVERT to float (invalid → NaN)
    DROP NaN rows
    RETURN clean DataFrame

Writing pseudocode first forces you to think through the logic before dealing with Python syntax. It also makes bugs easier to spot — if the logic is wrong in pseudocode it will be wrong in code too.

